    "summary": "The handler runtime now takes RuntimeQueue/RuntimeIndexer interfaces instead of the concrete classes. codeIndexWorkFor may answer asynchronously, so codeReview.freshness awaits it, and collectRepoStats takes Pick<IndexQueue,'depthForRepo'>. Added IndexingPortClient (src/daemon/threads/indexing-port.ts). It reads depth, lanes and the sweep from the board, and turns enqueue, codeIndexWorkFor, addRepo and removeRepo into requests to the code-indexing worker through the new Router.request(cls, method, params, {underHold}). depthForRepo is answered only on the worker: its one caller, repo.stats, runs there. createInDaemonClient takes a route; a nested call to a method of a routed class goes to that class's worker, and a new request() method allows any unary nested call. With daemon.threads.enabled, main() now builds no IndexQueue, Watcher or IndexerService; it starts the code-indexing worker, routes indexing, and on shutdown pushes indexing.stop and waits for the drain. Single-thread behaviour is unchanged when the flag is off. A new boot test starts the real daemon entry with the flag on: it answers admin, indexing and session methods and shuts down on daemon.shutdown. Finding: the existing in-daemon client calls only session methods (workflow.review, codeReview.run/grounding/freshness, repo.resolveForCwd), so the routed path is reached through the new request().",
